Error [jet.MarkerLookupNotMarker]: `Point` is not a marker
  --> tests/ui/marker_lookup_refusals.jet:20:20
    |
 20 |     if info.marker(Point) != None -> found += 1
    |                    ^^^^^
 Why: `marker(T)` reads the marker `T` written on a reflected item, so `T` names a struct with an `impl Marker` block or a Prelude marker
 Fix: Name a marker struct visible here or a Prelude marker such as `Codable`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E1134

